[
  {
    "text": "The cartoon ran in every",
    "start": 0.03,
    "end": 1.29
  },
  {
    "text": "Hearst paper in America.",
    "start": 1.29,
    "end": 3.12
  },
  {
    "text": "A fat man in a",
    "start": 3.12,
    "end": 3.84
  },
  {
    "text": "suit covered in dollar signs,",
    "start": 3.84,
    "end": 5.68
  },
  {
    "text": "smoking a cigar the size",
    "start": 5.68,
    "end": 7.12
  },
  {
    "text": "of his forearm.",
    "start": 7.12,
    "end": 8.24
  },
  {
    "text": "The caption changed every week.",
    "start": 8.24,
    "end": 10.16
  },
  {
    "text": "The man did not.",
    "start": 10.16,
    "end": 11.36
  },
  {
    "text": "His name was Mark Hanna,",
    "start": 11.36,
    "end": 13.07
  },
  {
    "text": "and in 1896, he did",
    "start": 13.07,
    "end": 14.6
  },
  {
    "text": "something no one had ever",
    "start": 14.6,
    "end": 15.78
  },
  {
    "text": "done at that scale.",
    "start": 15.78,
    "end": 16.84
  },
  {
    "text": "He turned the American presidential",
    "start": 16.84,
    "end": 18.55
  },
  {
    "text": "election into a corporate purchase",
    "start": 18.55,
    "end": 20.34
  },
  {
    "text": "order, three and a half",
    "start": 20.34,
    "end": 21.55
  },
  {
    "text": "million dollars raised, 20 times",
    "start": 21.55,
    "end": 23.64
  },
  {
    "text": "what his opponent spent.",
    "start": 23.64,
    "end": 25.1
  },
  {
    "text": "Banks assessed at a quarter",
    "start": 25.1,
    "end": 26.94
  },
  {
    "text": "of a percent of capital,",
    "start": 26.94,
    "end": 28.68
  },
  {
    "text": "railroads shaken down personally, standard",
    "start": 28.71,
    "end": 31.8
  },
  {
    "text": "oil, $250,000.",
    "start": 31.8,
    "end": 33.68
  },
  {
    "text": "JP Morgan, $250,000, half a",
    "start": 34.08,
    "end": 38.06
  },
  {
    "text": "million voters transported by train",
    "start": 38.06,
    "end": 40.19
  },
  {
    "text": "to shake one man's hand,",
    "start": 40.19,
    "end": 41.64
  },
  {
    "text": "200 million pieces of campaign",
    "start": 41.64,
    "end": 43.36
  },
  {
    "text": "literature printed and mailed.",
    "start": 43.36,
    "end": 45.36
  },
  {
    "text": "The opposition had a 36-year-old",
    "start": 45.36,
    "end": 47.39
  },
  {
    "text": "preacher who could move a",
    "start": 47.39,
    "end": 48.87
  },
  {
    "text": "crowd to tears.",
    "start": 48.87,
    "end": 49.96
  },
  {
    "text": "Hanna had a ledger, and",
    "start": 49.96,
    "end": 51.48
  },
  {
    "text": "when November came, the ledger",
    "start": 51.48,
    "end": 53.08
  },
  {
    "text": "won.",
    "start": 53.08,
    "end": 53.36
  },
  {
    "text": "He wasn't born with money.",
    "start": 53.36,
    "end": 54.84
  },
  {
    "text": "He was born in a",
    "start": 54.87,
    "end": 55.8
  },
  {
    "text": "grocery, New Lisbon, Ohio, 1837.",
    "start": 55.8,
    "end": 59.16
  },
  {
    "text": "His father, Dr.",
    "start": 59.16,
    "end": 60.06
  },
  {
    "text": "Leonard Hanna, was a country",
    "start": 60.06,
    "end": 61.34
  },
  {
    "text": "physician who ran a wholesale",
    "start": 61.34,
    "end": 62.92
  },
  {
    "text": "grocery on the side, flour,",
    "start": 62.92,
    "end": 64.77
  },
  {
    "text": "salt, dry goods to Ohio",
    "start": 64.77,
    "end": 66.28
  },
  {
    "text": "farmers.",
    "start": 66.28,
    "end": 67.08
  },
  {
    "text": "When Mark was 15, the",
    "start": 67.08,
    "end": 68.43
  },
  {
    "text": "family moved to Cleveland.",
    "start": 68.43,
    "end": 70.04
  },
  {
    "text": "He enrolled at Western Reserve",
    "start": 70.04,
    "end": 71.97
  },
  {
    "text": "College.",
    "start": 71.97,
    "end": 72.4
  },
  {
    "text": "In his class was a",
    "start": 72.4,
    "end": 73.52
  },
  {
    "text": "quiet, awkward boy who would",
    "start": 73.52,
    "end": 75.37
  },
  {
    "text": "grow up to control 90%",
    "start": 75.37,
    "end": 77.08
  },
  {
    "text": "of the oil-refining capacity in",
    "start": 77.08,
    "end": 79.01
  },
  {
    "text": "the United States.",
    "start": 79.01,
    "end": 80.36
  },
  {
    "text": "His name was John D.",
    "start": 80.36,
    "end": 81.56
  },
  {
    "text": "Rockefeller.",
    "start": 81.56,
    "end": 82.56
  },
  {
    "text": "The two would orbit each",
    "start": 82.59,
    "end": 83.74
  },
  {
    "text": "other for the next 40",
    "start": 83.74,
    "end": 84.98
  },
  {
    "text": "years.",
    "start": 84.98,
    "end": 85.5
  },
  {
    "text": "Hanna lasted one year at",
    "start": 85.5,
    "end": 86.75
  },
  {
    "text": "Western Reserve before he quit,",
    "start": 86.75,
    "end": 88.48
  },
  {
    "text": "not because he was failing,",
    "start": 88.48,
    "end": 89.96
  },
  {
    "text": "because he had already figured",
    "start": 89.96,
    "end": 91.03
  },
  {
    "text": "out something the professors couldn't",
    "start": 91.03,
    "end": 92.85
  },
  {
    "text": "teach.",
    "start": 92.85,
    "end": 93.24
  },
  {
    "text": "The real education was in",
    "start": 93.24,
    "end": 94.59
  },
  {
    "text": "the price of things.",
    "start": 94.59,
    "end": 95.84
  },
  {
    "text": "He went back to the",
    "start": 95.84,
    "end": 96.68
  },
  {
    "text": "store, worked the floor, watched",
    "start": 96.68,
    "end": 98.62
  },
  {
    "text": "how men negotiated, watched who",
    "start": 98.62,
    "end": 100.59
  },
  {
    "text": "paid on time and who",
    "start": 100.59,
    "end": 101.65
  },
  {
    "text": "didn't, watched which suppliers had",
    "start": 101.65,
    "end": 103.68
  },
  {
    "text": "leverage and which ones begged.",
    "start": 103.68,
    "end": 105.36
  },
  {
    "text": "Then the Civil War came.",
    "start": 105.36,
    "end": 106.6
  },
  {
    "text": "He served briefly, came home,",
    "start": 106.6,
    "end": 108.8
  },
  {
    "text": "and married a woman named",
    "start": 108.8,
    "end": 110.01
  },
  {
    "text": "Charlotte Rhodes.",
    "start": 110.01,
    "end": 111.12
  },
  {
    "text": "Her father was Daniel Rhodes,",
    "start": 111.15,
    "end": 112.88
  },
  {
    "text": "coal and iron, one of",
    "start": 112.88,
    "end": 114.86
  },
  {
    "text": "the men quietly getting rich",
    "start": 114.86,
    "end": 116.45
  },
  {
    "text": "off everything Cleveland was becoming.",
    "start": 116.45,
    "end": 118.8
  },
  {
    "text": "Hanna walked into that business",
    "start": 118.8,
    "end": 120.1
  },
  {
    "text": "and never walked out.",
    "start": 120.1,
    "end": 121.44
  },
  {
    "text": "By 1867, Marcus Alonso Hanna",
    "start": 121.44,
    "end": 123.84
  },
  {
    "text": "had built M.A.",
    "start": 123.84,
    "end": 124.78
  },
  {
    "text": "Hanna and Company, a coal",
    "start": 124.78,
    "end": 126.38
  },
  {
    "text": "and iron brokerage, sitting at",
    "start": 126.38,
    "end": 128.49
  },
  {
    "text": "the exact pivot point where",
    "start": 128.49,
    "end": 130.1
  },
  {
    "text": "Lake Erie Ore Boats unloaded",
    "start": 130.1,
    "end": 131.76
  },
  {
    "text": "for the Pittsburgh Steel Mills.",
    "start": 131.76,
    "end": 133.36
  },
  {
    "text": "Cleveland was the choke point",
    "start": 133.36,
    "end": 135.07
  },
  {
    "text": "and Hanna sat on it.",
    "start": 135.07,
    "end": 136.28
  },
  {
    "text": "Every ton of iron ore",
    "start": 136.28,
    "end": 137.44
  },
  {
    "text": "that crossed Lake Erie in",
    "start": 137.44,
    "end": 138.53
  },
  {
    "text": "the 1870s passed through brokers",
    "start": 138.53,
    "end": 140.86
  },
  {
    "text": "like him.",
    "start": 140.86,
    "end": 141.56
  },
  {
    "text": "He took a cut, then",
    "start": 141.56,
    "end": 142.82
  },
  {
    "text": "he bought the newspaper, the",
    "start": 142.82,
    "end": 143.96
  },
  {
    "text": "Cleveland Herald, then a theater,",
    "start": 143.96,
    "end": 145.92
  },
  {
    "text": "then banking interests, then a",
    "start": 145.92,
    "end": 147.64
  },
  {
    "text": "streetcar line.",
    "start": 147.64,
    "end": 148.6
  },
  {
    "text": "By 1880, he controlled enough",
    "start": 148.6,
    "end": 150.27
  },
  {
    "text": "of Cleveland that when he",
    "start": 150.27,
    "end": 151.24
  },
  {
    "text": "walked into a room, the",
    "start": 151.24,
    "end": 152.26
  },
  {
    "text": "room changed temperature and he",
    "start": 152.26,
    "end": 154.18
  },
  {
    "text": "was bored.",
    "start": 154.18,
    "end": 154.88
  },
  {
    "text": "Not with money, he had",
    "start": 154.88,
    "end": 156.07
  },
  {
    "text": "money bored with the ceiling",
    "start": 156.07,
    "end": 157.8
  },
  {
    "text": "because Hanna had figured out.",
    "start": 157.8,
    "end": 159.18
  },
  {
    "text": "Watching the men who supplied",
    "start": 159.18,
    "end": 160.63
  },
  {
    "text": "his coal, the politicians who",
    "start": 160.63,
    "end": 162.25
  },
  {
    "text": "regulated his rail routes, the",
    "start": 162.25,
    "end": 163.95
  },
  {
    "text": "judges who settled his contracts,",
    "start": 163.95,
    "end": 165.8
  },
  {
    "text": "that money was the second",
    "start": 165.83,
    "end": 167.05
  },
  {
    "text": "most powerful thing in America.",
    "start": 167.05,
    "end": 168.8
  },
  {
    "text": "The most powerful thing was",
    "start": 168.8,
    "end": 170.1
  },
  {
    "text": "who decided where the money",
    "start": 170.1,
    "end": 171.74
  },
  {
    "text": "went.",
    "start": 171.74,
    "end": 171.92
  },
  {
    "text": "That was politics and no",
    "start": 171.92,
    "end": 173.4
  },
  {
    "text": "one had ever run it",
    "start": 173.4,
    "end": 174.2
  },
  {
    "text": "like a business.",
    "start": 174.2,
    "end": 175.08
  },
  {
    "text": "Not yet.",
    "start": 175.08,
    "end": 175.92
  },
  {
    "text": "The year was 1888.",
    "start": 175.92,
    "end": 177.84
  },
  {
    "text": "The Republican National Convention, Chicago.",
    "start": 177.84,
    "end": 180.96
  },
  {
    "text": "Mark Hanna arrived not as",
    "start": 180.96,
    "end": 182.32
  },
  {
    "text": "a candidate, but as a",
    "start": 182.32,
    "end": 183.52
  },
  {
    "text": "kingmaker.",
    "start": 183.52,
    "end": 184.24
  },
  {
    "text": "His man was John Sherman.",
    "start": 184.24,
    "end": 185.92
  },
  {
    "text": "Ohio senator, treasury veteran, the",
    "start": 185.92,
    "end": 188.38
  },
  {
    "text": "establishment choice.",
    "start": 188.38,
    "end": 189.76
  },
  {
    "text": "Hanna worked the convention floor",
    "start": 189.76,
    "end": 191.2
  },
  {
    "text": "for six days, trading delegates,",
    "start": 191.2,
    "end": 193.32
  },
  {
    "text": "promising postmasterships, calling in markers",
    "start": 193.32,
    "end": 196.1
  },
  {
    "text": "from Ohio to Pennsylvania.",
    "start": 196.1,
    "end": 197.88
  },
  {
    "text": "Sherman peaked on the first",
    "start": 197.88,
    "end": 199.81
  },
  {
    "text": "ballot at 229 votes.",
    "start": 199.81,
    "end": 201.54
  },
  {
    "text": "Then he bled out, ballot",
    "start": 201.54,
    "end": 203.05
  },
  {
    "text": "after ballot, until the nomination",
    "start": 203.05,
    "end": 204.89
  },
  {
    "text": "went to Benjamin Harrison on",
    "start": 204.89,
    "end": 206.48
  },
  {
    "text": "the 8th.",
    "start": 206.48,
    "end": 207.28
  },
  {
    "text": "Hanna lost, but he saw",
    "start": 207.28,
    "end": 208.76
  },
  {
    "text": "something that weak he would",
    "start": 208.76,
    "end": 210.06
  },
  {
    "text": "never forget.",
    "start": 210.06,
    "end": 210.84
  },
  {
    "text": "A 45-year-old congressman from Canton,",
    "start": 210.84,
    "end": 213.96
  },
  {
    "text": "Ohio, had been chairing the",
    "start": 213.96,
    "end": 215.2
  },
  {
    "text": "resolutions committee.",
    "start": 215.2,
    "end": 216.44
  },
  {
    "text": "When delegates began breaking toward",
    "start": 216.44,
    "end": 218.15
  },
  {
    "text": "him as a dark horse",
    "start": 218.15,
    "end": 219.16
  },
  {
    "text": "alternative, the congressman walked to",
    "start": 219.16,
    "end": 221.43
  },
  {
    "text": "the microphone and refused.",
    "start": 221.43,
    "end": 223.06
  },
  {
    "text": "He told the convention he",
    "start": 223.09,
    "end": 224.42
  },
  {
    "text": "was bound to Sherman and",
    "start": 224.42,
    "end": 225.8
  },
  {
    "text": "he sat down.",
    "start": 225.8,
    "end": 226.76
  },
  {
    "text": "That kind of loyalty was",
    "start": 226.76,
    "end": 228.21
  },
  {
    "text": "rare in 1888 politics.",
    "start": 228.21,
    "end": 230.4
  },
  {
    "text": "It was almost extinct.",
    "start": 230.4,
    "end": 231.96
  },
  {
    "text": "His name was William McKinley.",
    "start": 231.96,
    "end": 234.08
  },
  {
    "text": "Hanna walked across the floor",
    "start": 234.08,
    "end": 235.79
  },
  {
    "text": "and introduced himself.",
    "start": 235.79,
    "end": 236.9
  },
  {
    "text": "He didn't know it yet,",
    "start": 236.9,
    "end": 238.43
  },
  {
    "text": "but he had just found",
    "start": 238.43,
    "end": 239.45
  },
  {
    "text": "his president.",
    "start": 239.45,
    "end": 240.4
  }
]
